hing that cannot be proven current and portable rather than carrying stale state forward. If the replacement is purely observational or can run without affecting control decisions, it can be introduced gradually alongside the old service for comparison and validation. But if it participates in scheduling, failover, or any mission-critical decision path, the old service should stay in place until the new one has been proven equivalent under representative fault conditions and across the same timing and recovery scenarios. In practice, a parallel rollout is only allowed when the new service can be kept isolated from the authoritative path and rolled back immediately if its results diverge.",
